/-!
# Coset geometries with b > 2

The original F.8.1 hypotheses give the G.2 central closure (F.8.2) and the
actual F.7 coset geometry (F.8.3). The quotient irreducibility and conjugate
intersection condition force odd critical distance at least three (F.8.5).
The chosen critical geodesic then gives every subgroup and commutator
conclusion of F.8.7, with literal quotient centralizers and two-residuals.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
Section F.8, printed pp.315–317, PDF pp.326–328.
-/
